      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In 185 patients (106 with asthma and 79 with COPD) peak inspiratory flow (PIFR) without resistance and across valves of popular in Poland dry powder inhalers (DPI): Discus, Turbuhaler and Aerolizer were recorded. \"In-Check\" device was used for these purposes. Clement-Clarke principle of minimal and optimal PIFR for lung drug deposition was accepted. According to this principle the results were presented on the attached table: [table: see text] Almost all patients with asthma and COPD can use Discus effectively, for other DPI's \"In Check\" investigation is often necessary."},
